% holding-blocked: Replace the discovery search with an authorized link to the 1974 "Mannenberg" recording. The round has only been checked by the page's interval score (92%, no downbeat clash with two groups four bars apart), not heard with children: a Grade 3 choir teacher must trial the bar-5 entry, the sixteenth groups at the start tempo and the lyric fit, a second score reader must check the notation, and a South African jazz educator must review the listening context. The title was changed from "Cape Town Round" so the piece does not claim a place it does not come from; the lead should confirm the new title.
